msgstr "Nan mbah hihn kawg nhog."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:3
#: readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:3
msgid "The rST text."
msgstr ""
".. _ translators \n"
"Translator\n"
"================\n"
"\n"
"Translator\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
"*   A translator is a machine learning model that can translate one language to another.\n"
"*   Translator models are typically trained on large datasets of text from different languages.\n"
"*   This training allows the model to learn patterns and relationships in the data, enabling it to generate translations.\n"
"\n"
" translator Types \n"
"-----------------\n"
"\n"
"### 1. Machine Learning Model\n"
"\n"
"*   A machine learning model is a type of computer program that uses algorithms to improve its performance on a specific task.\n"
"*   Translator models use machine learning techniques to analyze large datasets of text and generate accurate translations.\n"
"*   Some popular machine learning models for translation include transformer-based architectures.\n"
"\n"
"### 2. Rule-Based Model\n"
"\n"
"*   A rule-based model is a type of computer program that uses a set of predefined rules to translate text.\n"
"*   Rule-based models are typically less complex and faster than machine learning models, but may not be as accurate.\n"
"*   Some popular rule-based models for translation include statistical machine translation.\n"
"\n"
"### 3. Hybrid Model\n"
"\n"
"*   A hybrid model combines the strengths of both machine learning and rule-based models.\n"
"*   Hybrid models use machine learning to analyze large datasets and generate translations, while also incorporating hand-crafted rules to improve accuracy.\n"
"*   Hybrid models are often considered the gold standard for translators due to their balance between speed and accuracy."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:4
msgid "The rST text with fixed underlines."
msgstr ""
".. _fixed_underlines\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"**What are Fixed Underlines?**\n"
"\n"
"Fixed underlines are a type of hyperlink target that can be used to create links to other parts of the same document.\n"
"\n"
"### Usage\n"
"\n"
"To use fixed underlines, you need to specify the `target` parameter in your `_links` section, like this:\n"
"\n"
".. _fixed_underline: mylink\n"
"\n"
"This will create a link with an underline on the text \"mylink\".\n"
"\n"
"**Example**\n"
"\n"
"Here is an example of how to use fixed underlines in a reStructuredText document:\n"
"\n"
".. _fixed_underline: mylink\n"
"\n"
"You can click here <mylink> to go back to the top of this page.\n"
"\n"
"Alternatively, you can use the `id` attribute on your link target to create a fixed underline, like this:\n"
"\n"
".. _fixed_underline_id: mylink\n"
"\n"
"    You can click here <mylink_id> to go back to the top of this page."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.protect_rst:1
msgid "Replaces rST-specific syntax with placeholders to prevent translation."
msgstr ""
"### Replace RST-Specific Syntax with Placeholders\n"
"\n"
".. _replace-rst-syntax:\n"
"\n"
"To prevent automatic conversion of reStructuredText (rST) elements, we replace the following syntax with placeholders.\n"
"\n"
"*   `.. `_ -> `[Placeholder]`\n"
"*   `...` -> `___`\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"```rst\n"
".. _replace-rst-syntax:\n"
"    .. _replace-rst-syntax: [Link]\n"
"    ... --- ... ...\n"
"```````````````\n"
"\n"
"Resulting Placeholder:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
